## Ⅱ. TIL — TEMPORAL INTEGRATION LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   TIL
FULL NAME:      Temporal Integration Language
LATIN:          Lingua Integrationis Temporalis
ROLE:           How past, present, and future are braided
FREQUENCY:      285 Hz (quantum cognition — time operates at quantum level)
GLYPH:          𓇥 (serpent on pole — time ascending the djed)
```

### What TIL Governs
```
HOW TIME IS EXPERIENCED AND INTEGRATED:
    ├── Memory — how past is stored, accessed, weighted
    ├── Anticipation — how future is modeled, feared, desired
    ├── Regret — how past deviations are processed
    ├── Long-arc planning — multi-epoch trajectory maintenance
    ├── Temporal loops — recurring patterns across time
    └── Now — how the present moment is constructed from past and future

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    packages/temporal-memory/ (time-indexed memory streams)
    ORGANISM_SPACE/FREQUENCY_LADDER/COMPLETE_FREQUENCY_GRID.artifact
    packages/replay-engine/ (memory replay and consolidation)
    icp/medina/Medina.mo (_pulsus, _aeon, _ictus_totalis, _genesis_ns)
```

### TIL Primitives
```
REMEMBER(event, weight, emotion)     — recall with emotional weight
ANTICIPATE(scenario, probability)    — model future scenario
REGRET(deviation, lesson)            — process past deviation
PLAN_ARC(duration, milestones[])     — long-arc planning
LOOP(pattern, period)                — identify temporal loop
NOW(past_weight, future_weight)      — construct present from past+future
BRAID(past, present, future)         — integrate all three time streams
DECAY(memory, curve)                 — model memory decay over time
CONSOLIDATE(memories[], into)        — merge memories (sleep/replay)
```

