## Ⅳ. RIL — REPAIR & INTEGRATION LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   RIL
FULL NAME:      Repair & Integration Language
LATIN:          Lingua Reparationis et Integrationis
ROLE:           Healing, reconciling contradictions, resolving conflicts
FREQUENCY:      528 Hz (transformation, DNA repair — literally healing)
GLYPH:          ☥ (ankh — the key of life, restoration)
```

### What RIL Governs
```
HOW THE SYSTEM HEALS ITSELF:
    ├── Self-healing — detecting and repairing internal damage
    ├── Refactoring — restructuring without losing identity
    ├── Forgiveness — releasing past failures from active state
    ├── Rollback + learn — reverting errors while retaining lessons
    ├── Contradiction resolution — reconciling opposing truths
    └── Integration — merging fragmented parts into wholeness

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    SECURITY.organism §7 (incident response: detect→contain→eradicate→recover→learn)
    packages/organism-kernel/ (OrganismState: MERGING, TERMINATED)
    GOVERNANCE.organism §8 (self-governance — recursive governance)
    src/organism/Heart.mo (rhythmIntegrity — detecting cardiac irregularity)
```

### RIL Primitives
```
DETECT(damage, location)           — find the break
CONTAIN(damage, boundary)          — prevent spread
HEAL(target, method)               — apply repair
REFACTOR(structure, preserving)    — restructure safely
FORGIVE(event, release)            — release from active state
ROLLBACK(to_state, retaining[])    — revert keeping lessons
RECONCILE(truth_a, truth_b)        — resolve contradiction
INTEGRATE(fragments[], into)       — merge parts into whole
SCAR(event, memory)                — healed but remembered
```

